  "live_records": {
    "q-53290": {
      "dom_id": "step-q53290",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14235533/assets/2772e28367d49fcf0e2503b7cdd5d5aae5ea217b7060b288f9fb6e149ee25f57.png)\n\nThe perimeter of the rectangle $LMNP$ above equals $22\\,cm.$ What is the length of $\\overset{―}{NP}?$",
      "worked_solution": "The opposite sides of a rectangle are congruent, so we have\n\n$$\nPL=MN=3\\,cm.\n$$\n\nFor the same reason, we also have\n\n$$\nNP=LM.\n$$\n\nNow, since the perimeter is $p=22\\,\\text{cm},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =LM+MN+NP+PL \\\\ 22 & =2NP+2PL \\\\ 22 & =2NP+6 \\\\ 16 & =2NP \\\\ 8 & =NP\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $NP=8\\,\\text{cm}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
