      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14235533/assets/b68ede517afc0d8fd6ce6a110ed261a805a3218d6afee3caaed88c73d6e3763e.png)\n\nFor which value of $t$ is the rectangle above also a square?",
      "worked_solution": "If $PQRS$ is a square, then $m∠RSQ={45}^{∘}.$ Now,  we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠RSQ & ={45}^{∘} \\\\ (6t+3)^{∘} & ={45}^{∘} \\\\ 6t & =42 \\\\ t & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
